WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:04.660
In the collective memory of the people, Diana,
Princess of Wales was everything a royal should

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.660
be.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.740
She was beautiful, composed, and full of compassion
for those in need.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:13.549
And when she died in 1997, it was a horrific
tragedy that shook the world.

00:00:13.549 --> 00:00:17.990
She had been robbed of a future that was looking
incredibly bright, and her sons would forever

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.370
be without a mother.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.900
But the dark secrets of Diana’s life prove
“all that glitters is not gold.”

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.930
Some people believe that her death was no
accident, and that it was actually an elaborate

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:36.760
conspiracy designed by the royal family to
silence her.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:50.199
Early Life
Diana was born on July 1, 1961, to John and

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:51.199
Frances Spencer.

00:00:51.199 --> 00:00:55.610
It had been tradition for members of the nobility
to marry one another for centuries, and her

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.870
parents were no exception.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:00.579
Together with her two older sisters and two
brothers, they lived in a mansion called Park

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:02.100
House in Norfolk, England.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.970
As you can imagine, Diana grew up with the
best things that money could buy, and she

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.960
went on playdates with children in the royal
family.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.790
But all of the money in the world can’t
buy happiness.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.860
John and Frances had a toxic marriage..

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.190
All her life, Diana’s parents never said
“I love you” to one another, or their

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:20.190
children.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.310
They pushed off most of the parental duties
on nannies and governesses.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.880
Her parents would eventually get a divorce
when she was 6.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.300
At age 9, her father sent her to boarding
school.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.140
Her mother remarried a man named Peter Shand
Kydd, who was the heir to a successful wallpaper

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.140
company.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.710
Her father married a woman named Raine McCorquodale,
who was the daughter of a famous romance novelist.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:40.420
The children were not present at their father’s
second marriage, and they had to find out

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:41.810
about it through in the newspaper.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:46.360
Diana and her siblings deeply resented Raine
as an “evil stepmother”, and blamed her

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.560
for tearing their happy family apart.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.140
Diana was a shy girl, and she struggled in
school.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.001
She was labeled as “the thick one” by
her family, and this was enough for her to

00:01:55.001 --> 00:01:57.950
end up crying in school every time she got
a bad grade.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:02.909
Deep down, all she really wanted was to be
loved and accepted for who she was, and dreamed

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:08.300
of a prince taking her away to live happily
ever after.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:15.690
Becoming a Princess
When she was just 16 years old, Diana met

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.280
Charles, Prince of Wales, for the first time.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.300
He was 29 and dating her older sister, Sarah.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.230
The relationship between Sarah and Charles
never went anywhere, so they went their separate

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.230
ways.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:29.510
However, Charles said that Diana made a big
impression on him, because he thought she

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.599
was very cheerful and beautiful.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:36.060
When she came of age, Diana could have chosen
to party like a socialite or travel the world

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.150
with her family’s wealth.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:42.270
But when she was 18, she chose the very normal
life of working as a kindergarten teacher.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.620
She used her own paychecks to share an apartment
with a few friends.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.160
Diana loved taking care of children, and it
made her very happy to give them the love

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.630
and encouragement that she never got as a
little girl.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.560
At that time, Diana was filled with a lot
of hope about her future.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.420
She said that she felt this deep sense of
destiny, and that one day, she would grow

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.319
up to do great things.

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:05.980
Prince Charles had been dating several women
over the years, including Camilla Rosemary

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:06.980
Shand.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.500
Camilla was not wife material in the eyes
of the Queen, so she abruptly married a multi-millionaire

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.980
named Andrew Parker-Bowles, instead.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:17.680
But Charles and Camilla had never actually
broken off their relationship, and they continued

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.730
having a secret affair the entire time she
was married.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:24.630
Charles was now in his 30’s, and under a
lot of pressure from his mother to settle

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:25.870
down and produce an heir.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:30.660
He needed a wife that was a member of the
aristocracy, and Diana had all of the qualifications

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.849
of a perfectly acceptable bride.

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:37.569
After going on only 13 dates, Charles proposed
to Diana when she was a barely-legal 18 year

00:03:37.569 --> 00:03:38.569
old.

00:03:38.569 --> 00:03:42.320
Even though they hardly knew one another,
Diana felt as though becoming the princess

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.280
was that sense of destiny that she had been
feeling all along.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.550
A couple weeks after their engagement, the
couple was interviewed by the press.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:52.180
Towards the very end, the reporter said that
they were both very much in love.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.800
Diana replied, “Of course!”

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.819
Charles laughed, saying, “Whatever ‘in
love means’.”

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:00.840
Watching the tape, you can clearly see that
Diana was heartbroken.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.879
In later interviews, Diana defines that instant
as the moment she knew that marrying him would

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:06.980
be a huge mistake.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:12.040
However, the entire world had their eyes on
her, and she knew it was her duty to go through

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.360
with the marriage.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.930
Even to this day, Diana and Charles still
go down in history for having one of the most

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.440
expensive weddings.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:23.910
Experts estimate that today, their wedding
would cost anywhere from $70 to $100 million.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.370
From the perspective of the people watching
the wedding on TV, it seemed like a dream

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:28.370
come true.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.330
Diana later said, “It was the worst day
of my life.”

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:36.910
Their honeymoon was on the Royal Yacht Britannia,
where Diana reportedly spent most of the time

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:37.910
sleeping.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:41.260
In 1982, Charles and Diana had been married
for less than a year, and she had already

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.520
discovered Charles’ secret relationship
with Camilla Parker-Bowles.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.300
He started to gaslight her, saying that she
was paranoid.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.570
This made her so devastated, that she threatened
to kill herself.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:53.790
Charles ignored her, and started to leave
to go on a horseback riding trip.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.610
Diana threw herself down the stairs.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.900
The Queen rushed to her aid, screaming for
a doctor.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.410
While all of the attendants surrounded the
princess, Charles kept walking.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:06.210
To the outside world, the marriage between
Diana and Charles seemed like a fairytale

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:07.330
had come to life.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.870
For the first time, people all around the
world were fascinated and invested in the

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:11.870
royal couple.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:17.000
No matter what was going on behind closed
doors, she had to smile, wave, and pretend

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.960
that everything was fine.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:26.750
The Secret Affairs
Diana was still just a teenager when she was

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:30.960
put under the pressure to be a perfect princess
in the media.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:35.350
Combined with her unhealthy marriage, it was
enough to make her spiral into a deep depression,

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:36.940
and she became bulimic.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:41.040
She had so much empathy for other people,
that a particularly difficult meeting visiting

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.850
the poor, sick, and wounded made her mental
health a lot worse.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:48.680
Instead of recognizing that she needed help,
Diana was treated like she a child throwing

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:52.750
a tantrum, and the royal family continued
to ignore her issues.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:55.160
William was born when Diana was 20 years old.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:58.960
Just barely out of her teenage years, she
was supposed to raise a future king.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.460
Little William brought a lot of joy and purpose
to her life.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.190
During interviews, the press would mostly
ignore her while they spoke with Charles,

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:09.070
and only ask Diana how the baby was doing.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:13.051
Even though this was actually very demeaning
to her, Diana’s face would light up, and

00:06:13.051 --> 00:06:16.330
she would gush about how much fun she was
having with him.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:21.800
Even after giving birth to the heir, her relationship
with her husband remained cold and distant.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:26.169
She eventually decided that if she was going
to be stuck in an unfaithful marriage, she

00:06:26.169 --> 00:06:27.460
would have an affair, too.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:31.520
When she was 23, Diana fell in love with a
cavalry officer named James Hewitt.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:35.170
They were together about a year before her
second son, Harry, was born.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:39.020
In pictures showing the two of them side-by-side,
it is easy to see why many people believe

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:43.400
that James Hewitt may be Prince Harry’s
biological father.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.350
This is such a popular theory, that it was
even turned into a stage play that was performed

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:48.449
on the West End.

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:52.139
Diana pushed Charles to be more involved in
raising the boys, instead of relying totally

00:06:52.139 --> 00:06:53.139
on nannies.

00:06:53.139 --> 00:06:54.139
She also wanted William and Harry to go to
school with other children.

00:06:54.139 --> 00:06:57.070
When the boys were old enough to go out, she
made sure they had normal experiences like

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:59.310
water parks, McDonald’s, and shopping.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.630
She also brought them to homeless shelters
to pass out hot tea and food.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:07.170
Prince Charles scoffed at these ideas, asking
why it was really necessary.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.830
When she was 25, Diana fell in love with her
bodyguard, Barry Mannakee.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.639
They became best friends, and she felt very
safe around him.

00:07:13.639 --> 00:07:18.320
He brought a lot of joy to her life, but Diana
claimed that they never actually crossed the

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:19.320
line.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:23.040
However, most people still consider this to
be an emotional affair at the very least.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.039
Once their friendship was revealed, Prince
Charles fired Mannakee.

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:30.220
Not long after leaving his job at the royal
palace, Barry Mannakee was killed in a motorcycle

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.220
accident.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.960
Charles told Diana were on their way to the
Cannes Film Festival in France when he told

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:35.960
her the news.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.410
Charles mentioned Mannakee’s death so casually,
it was as if he was talking about the weather.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:43.509
Diana wanted to cry, but she knew that within
just a few moments, she would have to step

00:07:43.509 --> 00:07:46.490
out of the car and be photographed by hundreds
of people.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:51.220
So, she had to put on a smile yet again, and
pretend like nothing was wrong.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.930
She later said, “I think he was bumped off….But
we’ll never know.”

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:59.010
Diana felt that if she did not escape the
marriage, she really just might take her own

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.010
life.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:03.900
She knew that her only hope at getting a divorce
would be to get the public on her side.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:09.639
So, she spoke with a journalist named Andrew
Morton about the truth of the dysfunctional

00:08:09.639 --> 00:08:10.639
household.

00:08:10.639 --> 00:08:15.139
Morton eventually publisher her biography
called Diana: Her True Story--In Her Own Words.

00:08:15.139 --> 00:08:19.900
For the first time in history, the public
got a glimpse into the life of a royal marriage,

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.990
and it wasn’t pretty.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:26.669
Charles responded by being interviewed for
a documentary in 1994 called Charles, The

00:08:26.669 --> 00:08:31.330
Private Man, The Public Role, where he admitted
to his affair with Camilla Parker-Bowles.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:35.659
Diana responded by doing an interview on BBC
Panorama in 1995.

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:39.990
During this interview, she said that she believed
Charles was not a good person, and he wasn’t

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.810
even fit to become the next King of the United
Kingdom.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:47.010
She believed that her son, William, would
do a much better job serving the people.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.200
Diana said of herself, “She won’t go quietly.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.820
That’s the problem.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:55.770
I’ll fight to the end.”

00:08:55.770 --> 00:09:01.360
Life After Divorce
Diana and Charles were seperated for years,

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:02.740
and were seeing other people.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:06.360
After the bickering back and forth in the
media, the Queen herself demanded that they

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.640
needed to officially get a divorce.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:13.230
In 1995, Diana began dating an Egyptian millionaire
named Dodi Fayed.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:17.130
His father was the owner of the successful
Harrods Department Store, and has the net

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:21.959
worth of $1.6 billion- (Which, for the record,
is far richer than the Queen herself.) Charles

00:09:21.959 --> 00:09:24.490
and Diana were officially divorced in 1996.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:28.980
Charles would eventually go on to marry his
long-time girlfriend Camilla Parker-Bowles.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:34.089
Even after leaving her position as Princess
of Wales, Diana wanted to continue her destiny

00:09:34.089 --> 00:09:36.370
by making a difference in the world.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:40.330
She was just terrible at public speaking,
which was necessary during charity events

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:41.930
and public appearances.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:46.140
She started to receive vocal lessons from
a former actor named Peter Settelen.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:49.630
During their lessons, Settelen set up a camera
to record her progress, and he also asked

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:51.900
her questions about her personal life.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.460
These became like much-needed therapy sessions
for her.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.230
She revealed secrets about her marriage, and
the royal family.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:01.580
Through these lessons with Settelen, she was
able to find her own voice, and learned to

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.220
thrive as a public speaker.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:06.900
After her death, those tapes were confiscated
by the royal family, and the public was not

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:09.310
able to see them until years later.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.820
Diana became a traditional celebrity.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:15.529
Without the benefit of royal security, the
paparazzi continued to follow her and write

00:10:15.529 --> 00:10:17.110
about her in the tabloids.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:21.440
Instead of allowing the press to only write
about her hair and fashion choices, she decided

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:25.810
to make the best of being in the spotlight
by getting involved in causes that mattered

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:26.810
to her.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:30.110
She raised awareness about the AIDS epidemic,
and traveled to several African countries

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:33.540
to fight for the end of landmines in public
spaces.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:37.890
One of the most famous photographs of her
was with a young amputee who had her leg blown

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:38.890
off.

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:43.110
Almost immediately after getting the attention
of the press, the laws about landmines were

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:44.110
changed.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.350
However, this was making a lot of politicians
unhappy.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:50.380
They said that she was getting involved in
issues she didn’t fully understand.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:53.210
Her response was that she truly didn’t care.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:56.839
She was going to fight for the people, and
not the politicians.

00:10:56.839 --> 00:11:01.089
Instead of wilting into quiet obscurity, Diana
was thriving.

00:11:01.089 --> 00:11:03.490
She was no longer bulimic or depressed.

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:07.190
She was glad to trade her title for a life
of freedom.

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:11.540
She auctioned off all of her designer gowns
and gave millions to charities she cared about.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:15.890
All of this only made the public love her
more, and she was still a princess in the

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:18.149
hearts of the people.

00:11:18.149 --> 00:11:25.140
The Mysterious Deaths
After her divorce was finalized, Diana was

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:27.630
dating an Egyptian man named Dodi Fayed.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:30.890
He was a multi-millionaire who lived a glamorous
life.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:34.269
Paparazzi took photos of them on vacations
around the world.

00:11:34.269 --> 00:11:37.080
The British press called him a “playboy”,
and wrote negative connotations about the

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:38.750
fact that he was muslim.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:42.850
He was actually a successful movie producer
who was best known for the Oscar-winning movie

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.350
Hook, starring Robin Williams.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:48.630
He was also the heir to the multi-billion
dollar Harrods Department Store fortune.

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:52.470
The two were very much in love, and they planned
on getting married.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:56.330
Some believe that Diana may have even been
pregnant with his child.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:59.910
If this was true, it would have caused a lot
of issues for the royal family.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:03.680
The idea that William and Harry could have
a muslim half-sibling was unacceptable.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:08.920
And she constantly threatened to reveal more
and more secrets to the press.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.860
Her charity work often interfered with money-making
schemes among the nobility, as well.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:16.779
She received death threats on a regular basis.

00:12:16.779 --> 00:12:20.760
Not long before her death, Diana wrote a letter
to her butler saying that she believed her

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:24.670
ex-husband Charles was trying to have her
killed in a car accident.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:29.100
She also called Dodi’s father, Mohamed Al
Fayed, and told him the same thing.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:34.860
On August 31, 1997, Dodi Fayed and Diana were
being driven through Paris by a man named

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.240
Henri Paul.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:39.620
Just as they entered the Alma Tunnel, they
were apparently running from the paparazzi,

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:41.070
and ended up in an accident.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:45.320
For whatever reason, every single one of the
security cameras inside of the tunnel just

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:49.990
so happened to not be working that day, so
there is no recording showing exactly what

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:50.990
happened.

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:56.180
According to witnesses, the car went into
a pole at 65 mph, and no one was wearing a

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.180
seat belt.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:01.420
On September the 6th, 1997, the streets of
London were lined with people mourning Princess

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:02.730
Diana’s death.

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:04.970
Millions tuned in to watch the funeral procession
on TV.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:09.250
The Royal Court held a trial, and found that
the crash was simply an accident.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:13.700
However, everyone present at that trial was
obligated to side with the royal family, and

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:17.390
their findings were totally biased.

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:22.740
In 1999, the French government investigated
the car crash, and came to the same conclusion

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.880
that it was simply an accident.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:30.579
However, in 2008, an new independent investigation
found that the driver, Henri Paul, had been

00:13:30.579 --> 00:13:34.260
heavily drinking that day, and the original
trial had failed to mention that.

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:38.350
They also concluded paparazzi vehicles were,
in fact, tailgating the car.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:42.060
The jury concluded that both Henri Paul was
responsible for the deaths, and that if he

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:44.410
was still alive, he would be convicted of
manslaughter.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:50.600
For some, this investigation was still not
enough for Dodi’s father, Mohamed Al Fayed.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.570
He spent years of his life struggling with
the racism while running his business, and

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:59.110
he was disgusted by how the media was portraying
Dodi, even though he was a victim, too.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:04.120
Mohamed Al Fayed claimed that he had evidence
for 175 separate conspiracy theories, and

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:08.010
paid for a documentary called Unlawful Killing
to cover them all.

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:11.920
Obviously, we can’t go too deep into all
of the conspiracy theories in this video,

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.950
but it was enough for the British government
to ban the documentary from being seen in

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:17.070
the United Kingdom.

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:21.390
According to these conspiracy theories, Henri
Paul was actually sober that day, because

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:25.060
the receipts from the hotel showed that he
only had two drinks at dinner, and he had

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:28.269
gone through a medical exam by security beforehand.

00:14:28.269 --> 00:14:32.560
He had actually outrun the paparazzi, and
a mysterious white Fiat Uno followed them

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:34.839
into the tunnel with a group of motorcycles.

00:14:34.839 --> 00:14:39.140
Some believe that these were MI6 agents who
were being paid by the government to kill

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.140
her.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:43.390
After inspecting the car, they discovered
that the seatbelts in Henri Paul’s car had

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:46.190
been tampered with, which is why no one was
wearing them.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:50.500
It took over an hour and a half for the ambulance
to get to the hospital, even though they were

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:51.670
nearby.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:55.329
Doctors believe that if Diana was wearing
her seatbelt and had gotten medical attention

00:14:55.329 --> 00:14:57.550
sooner, she would have survived.

00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:02.870
Unfortunately, without video tape of the crash,
we may never know the whole truth of the circumstances

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:04.410
surrounding her death.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:09.370
Today, Princess Diana is not truly gone, because
she lives on in Prince William and Harry’s

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:10.370
legacy.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:14.260
Because of her, they both do charitable work,
and they married for love, instead of finding

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:17.320
a mate inside of the royal family.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:33.439
If she could see them, she would surely be
proud.

